{
 "duration": 30.036313,
 "phrases": [
  {
   "text": "This Roman builder is about to ruin his concrete.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 2.968
  },
  {
   "text": "He tosses in burning-hot lime.",
   "start": 3.137,
   "end": 5.166
  },
  {
   "text": "It hisses...",
   "start": 5.327,
   "end": 6.031
  },
  {
   "text": "and leaves little white lumps all through the mix.",
   "start": 6.218,
   "end": 8.687
  },
  {
   "text": "Ha!",
   "start": 8.863,
   "end": 9.113
  },
  {
   "text": "Sloppy work!",
   "start": 9.308,
   "end": 10.331
  },
  {
   "text": "Two thousand years later, his sea wall is still standing...",
   "start": 10.488,
   "end": 13.831
  },
  {
   "text": "while the modern concrete beside it has crumbled.",
   "start": 13.993,
   "end": 16.339
  },
  {
   "text": "Then a crack opens.",
   "start": 16.522,
   "end": 17.927
  },
  {
   "text": "Seawater trickles in...",
   "start": 18.103,
   "end": 19.46
  },
  {
   "text": "and the crack begins to seal itself.",
   "start": 19.636,
   "end": 21.508
  },
  {
   "text": "Those lumps were tiny pockets of lime.",
   "start": 21.669,
   "end": 23.978
  },
  {
   "text": "Water dissolves them, and they refill the crack with fresh stone.",
   "start": 24.147,
   "end": 27.442
  },
  {
   "text": "Roman concrete...",
   "start": 27.617,
   "end": 28.776
  },
  {
   "text": "heals itself.",
   "start": 28.948,
   "end": 29.911
  }
 ],
